  "title": "Accusative Case (Intro)",
  "titleRussian": "Винительный падеж (введение)",
  "description": "Accusative case for direct objects (inanimate focus)",
  "descriptionRussian": "Винительный падеж для прямых дополнений (неодушевлённые)",
  "imageName": "arrow.right.circle.fill",
  "intro": "The accusative case (винительный падеж) marks the direct object - the thing receiving the action. When you read a book, 'book' is the direct object. In Russian, nouns change their endings to show they're direct objects. This lesson focuses on inanimate nouns (things, not people/animals).",
  "rules": [
    "Accusative marks the direct object - the thing receiving the action: Я читаю книгу.",
    "Inanimate masculine and ALL neuter nouns: accusative = nominative (no change): стол → стол, окно → окно.",
    "Feminine nouns ending in -а: change to -у: книга → книгу, мама → маму.",
    "Feminine nouns ending in -я: change to -ю: песня → песню, неделя → неделю."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Я читаю книгу. (I am reading a book.), книга → книгу",
    "Он видит стол. (He sees the table.), стол stays стол (masc. inanimate)",
    "Мы смотрим фильм. (We are watching a film.), фильм stays фильм",
    "Она слушает музыку. (She is listening to music.), музыка → музыку"
  ],
